{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QResolventUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QResolventUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysis"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QResolvent.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QResolvent.unique","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent-unique.lean#L35-L50","doc":"**Uniqueness of the q-resolvent (proved, conditional on\nsurjectivity).**\n\nTwo `QResolvent H` instances with the same q-Laplacian `delta_q`\nhave the same resolvent `R`, provided `delta_q` is surjective: on\n`delta_q x` the inverse witness gives `R (delta_q x) = x` for both.\nThis replaces an unchecked external axiom with the determination\nthe inverse witness genuinely provides. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-resolvent-unique","label":"prop:q-resolvent-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-resolvent-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}